properties.description:
skill_lint's ANSWER_FIRST_CONTRACT (tools/skill_lint.py, run in CI on every push, with its own tests in tools/test_skill_lint.py) pins six clauses in getting-started/skills/brainstorm/SKILL.md:
- look for the answer before framing a question as open;
- search accepted intent, not only ideas;
- read the project's statement of what it is for;
- an answered question is not a brainstorm;
- never offer a settled road as a live option;
- route a wish to revisit through the settled node.
The same lint holds the .claude and .grok mirrors byte-identical to the source. What it cannot check is whether an agent actually searches. That is judgement, and it stays evidenced by real use, as the file header says for every contract.
